    "en": "Levels of biodiversity"
   },
   "tex": "\\text{genetic (Rauwolfia, reserpine)};\\ \\text{species (W. vs E. Ghats amphibians)};\\ \\text{ecological (India vs Norway)}",
   "note": {
    "en": "Term popularised by Edward Wilson. India: >50,000 rice strains, 1000 mango varieties."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "zs-f2",
   "topicId": "puc2-biology-13-biodiversity-and-conservation.t1",
   "name": {
    "en": "Global species counts"
   },
   "tex": "\\text{described} > 1.5 \\text{ million (IUCN 2004)};\\ \\text{May's estimate} \\approx 7 \\text{ million}",
   "note": {
    "en": "Insects >70% of animals (7 in 10)."
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "zs-f3",
   "topicId": "puc2-biology-13-biodiversity-and-conservation.t1",
   "name": {
    "en": "India's share"
